  "agent": "KW Peninsula Estates",
  "text": "A condo alternative with no HOA dues. This VACANT charming attached single-family home may be one of the smallest houses in San Francisco. It's a rare chance to own a house of your own without stretching your budget. Built in 1955, the two-level home has an open kitchen and living area on the lower level. It has tile floors, wood cabinets, an electric cooktop with a range hood, and a large street-facing window. A closet holds a stacked washer and dryer, which are included in the sale. Upstairs, the bedroom has hardwood floors, a bay window that brings in plenty of light, a closet and a wall air-conditioning unit. The bathroom has a glass-enclosed shower and a skylight. The home is a good fit for anyone hoping to live and work in one place. Buyers should check with the city on what uses are allowed. Street parking only. You're close to the Mission and Valencia Street corridors, with their restaurants, cafes and shops, and within walking distance of BART, with easy freeway access. The home borders Noe Valley, Bernal Heights and the Mission, an ideal spot to live and work in vibrant San Francisco.",
