  "sqft": 1085,
  "rating": "",
  "agent": "Compass",
  "text": "Victorian character and fresh modern touches meet at 2758 22nd Street, a bright 3 bedroom / 1.5 bathroom condo in the Inner Mission. A front-gabled facade with decorative cornices and ornamental trim, complemented by a lush magnolia, gives the building a distinctive presence on its quiet tree-lined block. The front-facing living room's bay windows welcome bright southern light, while a fireplace with an ornate columned mantel and tiled surround anchors the room. Other period touches seen here repeat throughout the home, including softwood floors, coved ceilings, decorative molding, and ceiling medallions. A hall closet with built-in bureau adds convenience. Along the central hallway, lined with anaglypta wall coverings, the first bedroom offers flexibility with a pocket-door connection to the living room, while the second, near the back of the home, features built-in closet shelving. Both enjoy direct access to an updated Jack-and-Jill bathroom with subway and mosaic tilework, plus radiant floor heating and a built-in storage cabinet. A third bedroom across the hall features elegant built-ins, a closet, and a window nook perfectly sized for a desk. At the rear, the extensively renovated eat-in kitchen boasts quartz countertops, generous cabinet and prep space, and stainless-steel appliances including a refrigerator, gas range, and dishwasher. The adjoining sunroom holds a washer/dryer and storage, plus access to a half bath and the shared yard, with a covered deck, brick-paved patio, and mature landscaping, including a fruit-bearing avocado tree. The garage provides 1-car tandem parking and ample private storage. Beyond the home, local restaurants, cafes, bars, shops, and nightlife thrive along Mission, Valencia, and 24th Streets. From casual takeout to Michelin stars, book shelves to movie screens, vanilla lattes to espresso martinis you can find it all in the Mission! BART and 24-hour Muni service are close by, earning Excellent Transit from, which also rates this location a Walker's + Biker's Paradise. With so much close at hand, 2758 22nd Street is an ideal urban retreat.",
