  "text": "Noe Valley living at its best, right off Elizabeth Street, just one block from 24th Street, with coffee shops, neighborhood dining, and groceries all just steps away. Set on the first floor of a boutique building, this bright corner condo has the kind of charm that feels distinctly San Francisco. Multiple windows fill the living room with natural light, hardwood floors lend warmth throughout, and a brick-framed fireplace creates an inviting centerpiece. A true one-bedroom layout offers a separate living room, kitchen, and bedroom, giving each space a comfortable sense of its own. The kitchen has plenty of personality, with Carrara marble counters, a Heath Ceramics tile backsplash, stainless steel appliances, and a gas range, plus ample room for a table and chairs. The bedroom offers a generous closet, while mosaic marble tile flooring adds character to the bathroom, complete with a shower over tub. The home also includes deeded storage and access to complimentary shared laundry. Morning coffee around the corner, Saturday farmer's market, all errands on foot, dinner on 24th Street, this is an easy home to imagine living in. A bright, charming retreat in one of Noe Valley's most desirable locations.",
